sieve-filter-v2
; Sentence shape, for pages of printable ASCII: punctuation and capitals where sentences put
; them. , ; : follow a word (or a closing bracket or quote) and are followed by a SPACE or a
; closer; . ! ? the same, up to three in a row ("...", "?!"), and a single . may be followed
; at once by a letter or digit ("e.g.", "U.S.", "3.14"); no SPACE before any of them. A
; capital starts a word or follows a capital ("HELLO"), never a small letter ("hEllo").
; With `capitals`, the first word after . ! ? and a SPACE starts with a capital (or a digit
; or bracket), which abbreviations such as "e.g. the" break. Brackets and quotes open after a
; SPACE and close after a word; a hyphen joins words ("well-known"), and two make a dash.
; The symbols # $ % & * + / < = > @ \ ^ _ ` { | } ~ count as
; letters when `others` allows them, and fail the page otherwise. A page can start and stop
; anywhere, so its first characters are judged as if anything came before them.
; Generated by tools/build_text_plugins.py (a machine over the characters, made deterministic).
id        sentence-shape
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   ascii95
describe  Punctuation and capitals where sentences put them (pages of printable ASCII).
param     capitals  choice  yes  no,yes  whether a sentence's first word starts with a capital
param     others    choice  no   no,yes  whether # $ % & * + / and the like may appear (as letters)

states    {(capitals == 1) * 38 + (capitals == 0) * 38}
start     0
accept    0..{(capitals == 1) * 37 + (capitals == 0) * 37}
if {capitals == 1}
  t 0 " " 1
  t 0 "!" 2
  t 0 "\"" 3
  t 0 "0123456789" 4
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "#" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "$" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "%" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "&" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "*" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "+" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "/" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "<" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "=" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 ">" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "@" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "\\" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "^" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "_" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "`" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "{" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "|" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "}" 4
  fi
  if {others == 1}
    t 0 "~" 4
  fi
  t 0 "'" 5
  t 0 "([" 6
  t 0 ")]" 7
  t 0 ",:;" 8
  t 0 "-" 9
  t 0 "." 10
  t 0 "?" 11
  t 0 "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ" 12
  t 0 "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz" 13
